# Careful: pnpm reads npm's `package-lock` key as an alias for its own `lockfile`
# setting. This file used to contain `package-lock=false`, which silently prevented
# pnpm from writing pnpm-lock.yaml at all. Do not reintroduce it — the lockfile is
# committed and CI installs with --frozen-lockfile.
#
# package-lock.json and yarn.lock stay in .gitignore, so using the wrong package
# manager locally still can't pollute the repo.
